.TH ICED\-LIBADWAITA\-META\-COMPONENT 3 "" "iced-libadwaita 0.1.0" "iced-libadwaita Manual"
.SH NAME
meta_component \- See the module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
MetaComponent::new()
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBMetaComponent\fR: it owns no content; it chooses \fBwhich presentation\fR (variant) of one piece of content to build, and builds only that one. Each variant has a key, a \fBTrigger\fR and a closure that builds it. The first whose trigger fires wins; the last is the fallback.
.PP
Triggers:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbreakpoint\fR: \fBTrigger::Breakpoint\fR (made from a \fBWhen\fR) fires by the size of the *container* the component sits in, not the window;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBselect\fR: \fBTrigger::Selected\fR fires while the application has selected a key (\fBselected\fR, controlled state), e.g. a search button;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgroups\fR: \fB|\fR (any), \fB&\fR (all) and \fB!\fR (not) combine triggers, so a variant can answer to several things at once. There can be any number of alternatives, one trigger each.
.PP
Other components are this one with their variants filled in:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBResponsiveTable\fR: a table while the columns fit, cards otherwise;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSidebarList\fR with \fBcards_below\fR: compact rows, or cards.
.PP
.nf
.RS
MetaComponent::new()
    .selected(self.searching.then_some(Bar::Search))      // on\-select trigger
    .when_selected(Bar::Search, |_| search_entry())
    .variant(Bar::Compact, Trigger::selected(Bar::Menu) | !wide, |_| menu())  // a group
    .variant(Bar::Path, When::always(), |_| path_bar())   // fallback
.RE
.fi
.PP
The choice is the pure function \fBMetaComponent::pick\fR over \fBprimitives::meta\fR. Like \fBresponsive\fR, the result fills its container by default.
